2025-05-01 01:21:35 - Thread-292 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• "place_geom": polygon geometry for each place – used to define Philadelphia’s boundary.  
• "place_name": literal name of the place – used to filter to Philadelphia.  
• "geometry": point geometry of every OpenStreetMap feature – used to measure distance.  
• "all_tags": JSON‑like VARIANT that stores key/value attribute pairs – used to locate amenities with key = ‘amenity’ and value in (‘library’, ‘place_of_worship’, ‘community_centre’).  
• "osm_id": OpenStreetMap unique identifier – helps keep the amenities distinct.  


Typical conditions you will combine  
• In the census‑place table: WHERE "place_name" ILIKE '%Philadelphia%'  
• In the OSM‑point table (after FLATTEN on "all_tags"):   
  WHERE key = 'amenity' AND value ILIKE ANY ('%library%', '%place_of_worship%', '%community_centre%')  
• Join condition for spatial containment:   
  ST_CONTAINS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(phil."place_geom"), TO_GEOGRAPHY(poi."geometry") )


Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (LIMIT 20 rows each) that progressively inspect the data, isolate the amenities inside Philadelphia, and finish by computing the single shortest inter‑amenity distance.  
All column names are wrapped in double quotes, and comments explain every step.

```sql
-- 1. Description:  Show all Pennsylvania place names that begin with “Phil” to verify Philadelphia’s exact entry.
SELECT DISTINCT "place_name"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES.PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA
WHERE "place_name" ILIKE 'Phil%' 
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description:  Retrieve the geometry polygon for the Philadelphia place boundary.
SELECT "place_id",
       "place_name",
       "place_geom"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES.PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA
WHERE "place_name" ILIKE '%Philadelphia%' 
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description:  Peek at the key/value structure inside the "all_tags" VARIANT for random OSM points.
SELECT "osm_id",
       f.value:"key"::STRING        AS tag_key,
       f.value:"value"::STRING      AS tag_value
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( input => p."all_tags" ) f
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description:  List the distinct values that appear with key = 'amenity' to see spelling/formatting.
SELECT DISTINCT f.value:"value"::STRING AS amenity_value
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( input => p."all_tags" ) f
WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description:  Pull all OSM point rows whose amenity is library, place_of_worship, or community_centre.
SELECT p."osm_id",
       f.value:"value"::STRING AS amenity_type,
       p."geometry"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( input => p."all_tags" ) f
WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING   = 'amenity'
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%library%', '%place_of_worship%', '%community_centre%')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description:  Join the amenities to Philadelphia’s polygon to keep only points that fall inside the city.
SELECT poi."osm_id",
       poi_amenity.tag_value   AS amenity_type,
       poi."geometry"
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS      poi,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( input => poi."all_tags" ) poi_amenity,
     GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES.PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA       phil
WHERE phil."place_name" ILIKE '%Philadelphia%'
  AND poi_amenity.value:"key"::STRING   = 'amenity'
  AND poi_amenity.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%library%','%place_of_worship%','%community_centre%')
  AND ST_CONTAINS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(phil."place_geom"),
                   TO_GEOGRAPHY(poi."geometry") )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description:  Show coordinates (longitude, latitude) for the first few Philadelphia amenities.
SELECT poi."osm_id",
       poi_amenity.tag_value           AS amenity_type,
       ST_X( TO_GEOGRAPHY(poi."geometry") ) AS lon,
       ST_Y( TO_GEOGRAPHY(poi."geometry") ) AS lat
FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS poi,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( input => poi."all_tags" ) poi_amenity,
     GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES.PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA phil
WHERE phil."place_name" ILIKE '%Philadelphia%'
  AND poi_amenity.value:"key"::STRING   = 'amenity'
  AND poi_amenity.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%library%','%place_of_worship%','%community_centre%')
  AND ST_CONTAINS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(phil."place_geom"),
                   TO_GEOGRAPHY(poi."geometry") )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description:  Pair every amenity with every other amenity inside Philadelphia (excluding self‑pairs) and compute distance in meters.
SELECT a."osm_id"                       AS amenity_id_a,
       b."osm_id"                       AS amenity_id_b,
       ST_DISTANCE(
           TO_GEOGRAPHY(a."geometry"),
           TO_GEOGRAPHY(b."geometry")
       )                                AS distance_meters
FROM (
        SELECT poi."osm_id", poi."geometry"
        FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS poi,
             LATERAL FLATTEN( input => poi."all_tags" ) f,
             GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES.PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA phil
        WHERE phil."place_name" ILIKE '%Philadelphia%'
          AND f.value:"key"::STRING   = 'amenity'
          AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%library%','%place_of_worship%','%community_centre%')
          AND ST_CONTAINS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(phil."place_geom"),
                           TO_GEOGRAPHY(poi."geometry") )
     ) a
JOIN (
        SELECT poi."osm_id", poi."geometry"
        FROM GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS poi,
             LATERAL FLATTEN( input => poi."all_tags" ) f,
             GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES.PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA phil
        WHERE phil."place_name" ILIKE '%Philadelphia%'
          AND f.value:"key"::STRING   = 'amenity'
          AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%library%','%place_of_worship%','%community_centre%')
          AND ST_CONTAINS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(phil."place_geom"),
                           TO_GEOGRAPHY(poi."geometry") )
     ) b
ON a."osm_id" < b."osm_id"   -- prevents duplicate & self matches
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description:  Order the amenity pairs by ascending distance to glimpse the smallest values.
SELECT *
FROM (
      /* Re‑using the distance computation from Query 8 */
      SELECT a."osm_id"               AS amenity_id_a,
             b."osm_id"               AS amenity_id_b,
             ST_DISTANCE(
                 TO_GEOGRAPHY(a."geometry"),
                 TO_GEOGRAPHY(b."geometry")
